Skills and Abilities
Ninjas do not passivly gain abilities as they gain guild levels.
Instead, a ninja must <practice> an ability before they can use it.
This is done through practice points. Ninjas start with 10 
practice points, and gain some additional points with every
<guild level>. Eventually, a Ninja can earn a maximum of 100
practice points. Training begins at 25% success and each additional
practice point increases the percentage by 10%, up to a maximum of
95%. This percentage determines how often a Ninja can use an ability
without failing. Currently, a Ninja has enough practice points to fully
practice all skills.

Upon reaching guild level 15 and guild level 20, a Ninja can
<master> an ability. This can only be done to skills practiced
up to rank 8. Mastering an ability increases the chance of successfully
using it to 100%.

Many offensive techniques also add a piece to the Ninja combo system.
When enough recent pieces are present, the wraps may release a special
combat sequence. See <ninhelp combo> for details.
